{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change","id":1345779,"title":"Intimacies and how commonly do they change","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-04T09:12:00-08:00","id":1345779,"title":"Intimacies and how commonly do they change","content":"Hi all.<br /> <br /> I am getting pumped for my first Exalted game to GM. But I have a query about intimacies. How often do they change in your games? From the rules its certainly possible for PCs and NPCs to change them deliberately and no dobut the PCs will create new ones, and lose old ones due to the events in game. How common is this in your games? Do you see it happen every session? Does it only happen commonly for the minor intimacies? Are changes of major or defining intimacies crowning moments of a session? Do tell!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:18:17-08:00","id":1345782,"title":"","content":"&quot;Four&quot; sessions in to my game and the only Intimacy which has changed has been a retcon.<br /> <br /> I think The Fall of Jiara had one NPC attempt to Instill an Intimacy so far and they're 17 sessions in. (I think the PC spent WP to resist it.)<br /> <br /> Generally speaking you don't need to &quot;work&quot; the social system to motivate PCs. Throw a disadvantaged orphan to the PCs and they'll just take inconvenient tasks to help the poor tyke out without having to Instill an official Intimacy.<br /> <br /> That said, these are Dragon-Blooded games, so less of a need to create new Intimacies, maybe? And maybe the PCs should take an Intimacy toward the random orphans they're helping out, I don't know if just helping without an Intimacy is working as intended or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-04-2019, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:29:44-08:00","id":1345784,"title":"","content":"Most of the changes to my Intimacies have come from fellow PCs; admittedly, part of that\u2019s been from people not being able to suss out what said Intimacies <i>are</i>. I\u2019m just too good at hiding them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:30:37-08:00","id":1345786,"title":"","content":"For my games, Minor Intimacies come and go relatively often, while Major Intimacies are rather difficult to create or erode. I don't think I've seen Defining Intimacies getting formed or eroded in any game, they often... well, define a character, so you don't want them to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:56:56-08:00","id":1345793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345784#post1345784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the changes to my Intimacies have come from fellow PCs; admittedly, part of that\u2019s been from people not being able to suss out what said Intimacies <i>are</i>. I\u2019m just too good at hiding them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the biggest problems with 3E is Instilling Intimacies. I think it should work more like Inspire -- you decide what you're doing, the target decides how they react.<br /> <br /> If your female presenting character acts promiscuous to try to Instill an Intimacy of Lust in my conservative gay male character and gets a bunch of successes, I should get an Intimacy of Revulsion (or Pity) instead of &quot;Red Rule, nothing happens&quot;.<br /> <br /> Finding out what people's Intimacies are, then how to leverage them to your advantage is way harder than just giving them new Intimacies that support what you want them to do. (IDK, in theory -- hasn't really come up in play for me yet.)<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't work out what you care about, so care about this new thing instead&quot; shouldn't be a viable option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:59:53-08:00","id":1345795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345793#post1345793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the biggest problems with 3E is Instilling Intimacies. I think it should work more like Inspire -- you decide what you're doing, the target decides how they react.<br /> <br /> If your female presenting character acts promiscuous to try to Instill an Intimacy of Lust in my conservative gay male character and gets a bunch of successes, I should get an Intimacy of Revulsion (or Pity) instead of &quot;Red Rule, nothing happens&quot;.<br /> <br /> Finding out what people's Intimacies are, then how to leverage them to your advantage is way harder than just giving them new Intimacies that support what you want them to do. (IDK, in theory -- hasn't really come up in play for me yet.)<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't work out what you care about, so care about this new thing instead&quot; shouldn't be a viable option.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can already do this. First, Red Rule the seduction out. Then, ask the ST if you can form an Intimacy at the end of the scene expressing revulsion or pity or w/e for her, there's rules for this. Imo, making people care about new things is perfectly fine, not everyone takes Socialize and Guile-monsters can be a pain so you just work extra hard to convince someone enough that they'll help you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:21:01-08:00","id":1345804,"title":"","content":"In kind of the same way that the exalted combat engine isn\u2019t supposed to map perfectly to a description of how things physically work in Exalted, the intimacy system isn\u2019t really supposed to be huge and comprehensive. Characters do things all the time that that may not have intimacies for. Just because you have an opinion about somebody doesn\u2019t rise that opinion to the level of even a minor intimacy. <br /> <br /> For my part in my games intimacies tend to go through changes at big campaign defining moments, like a big reveal of betrayal or loyalty, or in any scene where a character, player or otherwise, is flexing their social abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:25:05-08:00","id":1345806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345795#post1345795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can already do this. First, Red Rule the seduction out. Then, ask the ST if you can form an Intimacy at the end of the scene expressing revulsion or pity or w/e for her, there's rules for this. Imo, making people care about new things is perfectly fine, not everyone takes Socialize and Guile-monsters can be a pain so you just work extra hard to convince someone enough that they'll help you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instilling new intimacies is always dodgy anyway, from what I recall it\u2019s always possible to no-sell the introduction of new intimacies with a willpower. Obviously using willpower to constantly block characters influence attempts is kind of dickish but that mechanic doesn\u2019t exist for no reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:36:22-08:00","id":1345811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345795#post1345795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can already do this. First, Red Rule the seduction out. Then, ask the ST if you can form an Intimacy at the end of the scene expressing revulsion or pity or w/e for her, there's rules for this. Imo, making people care about new things is perfectly fine, not everyone takes Socialize and Guile-monsters can be a pain so you just work extra hard to convince someone enough that they'll help you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that something should happen.<br /> <br /> If you try to sell me a yeddim, I should either buy the yeddim, come away thinking you're a pushy salesman I want nothing to do with, or both. <br /> <br /> Straight-up &quot;no selling&quot; an Instill role seems kinda... cheesy. &quot;You roll 23 success. Nothing happens.&quot; I'd rather <i>something</i> happen, and I'd rather Solar mind-control wasn't a thing and that people had to actually engage with what your character cares about rather than rewriting you with new Intimacies.<br /> <br /> Guile should do something. If you're invested in hiding what you care about that should have a benefit. If you're bad at reading people that should have an effect on your ability to convince people to do what you want.<br /> <br /> But, again, this has only ever been a theorycraft problem. In play it works ok, and I acknowledge the rules you pointed out do exist.<br /> <br /> Working extra hard to get someone to help you is fine. Working extra hard to force someone to help you is less fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-04-2019, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:43:32-08:00","id":1345812,"title":"","content":"In play, Intimacies are like badges or keepsakes of what happens to your character. You create a Tie of Hatred when you meet a despicable villain, take up a new principle when something changes your worldview, and so on. No one gets their PC's intimacies right on the first try, so it's good to revise them every few games.<br /> <br /> Social influence is extremely powerful, but having your character changed without your consent is rarely fun, so unless the PCs all want to play a game where their character's personality can be turned inside out on a whim, social influence is usually limited to local events/people rather than the core of your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:51:31-08:00","id":1345815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345806#post1345806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Instilling new intimacies is always dodgy anyway, from what I recall it\u2019s always possible to no-sell the introduction of new intimacies with a willpower. Obviously using willpower to constantly block characters influence attempts is kind of dickish but that mechanic doesn\u2019t exist for no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Willpower is encouraged to only ever be spent when there are big Intimacies going against the Influence; it's primarily an anti-frustration tech for PCs, while the ST should look at the NPC's Intimacies to determine whether not caring about something is so important that they would spend a precious resource on it, particularly for Mortals who often only have 3 permanent WP. Also, Decision Points existing means that once you do instill an Intimacy and leverage it, it becomes harder than just &quot;spend WP&quot; to resist the leverage. Ditto with Overturning Influence rules and other such ones. So nah, it's not really dodgy, it is context-dependent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:51:47-08:00","id":1345816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345786#post1345786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my games, Minor Intimacies come and go relatively often, while Major Intimacies are rather difficult to create or erode. I don't think I've seen Defining Intimacies getting formed or eroded in any game, they often... well, define a character, so you don't want them to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my experience too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To the OP, one thing to note is that if a minor intimacy is instilled in a PC, it shouldn't normally vanish for a couple of sessions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T11:20:22-08:00","id":1345823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345793#post1345793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your female presenting character acts promiscuous to try to Instill an Intimacy of Lust in my conservative gay male character and gets a bunch of successes, I should get an Intimacy of Revulsion (or Pity) instead of &amp;quot;Red Rule, nothing happens&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the Red Rule, that's just... the rule. &quot;Any seduction attempt that violates a character's sexual orientation (as defined by the player, or by the Storyteller in the case of Storyteller characters) is unacceptable [influence]&quot;.<br /> <br /> Playing a failed social action as forming a contrary Intimacy to represent a lowered opinion is fine, but folding that into the general social system seems far too unwieldy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T11:39:22-08:00","id":1345827,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like intamacies to come and go, change, and evolve constantly. The social systems are built for it. It isn't happening you aren't really engaging with the social systems very much. That's fine for a lot of groups. A lot of players come from the traditional view of roleplaying where your character and everything they do is in your head and if you dont want your character to do or feel something they dont.<br /> <br /> Exalted's social rules encourage characters to grow and change in unexpected ways and players to adapt to the changes their characters go through. I like this because I'm actually kinda shit at RP, so intimacies provide me solid cues for what a character is feeling and thinking and serve as good rp queues. I also really enjoy exploring characters growing and changing through the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:25:16-08:00","id":1345845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345815#post1345815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower is encouraged to only ever be spent when there are big Intimacies going against the Influence; it's primarily an anti-frustration tech for PCs, while the ST should look at the NPC's Intimacies to determine whether not caring about something is so important that they would spend a precious resource on it, particularly for Mortals who often only have 3 permanent WP. Also, Decision Points existing means that once you do instill an Intimacy and leverage it, it becomes harder than just &amp;quot;spend WP&amp;quot; to resist the leverage. Ditto with Overturning Influence rules and other such ones. So nah, it's not really dodgy, it is context-dependent.</div> </div> </div> </div>But...you\u2019ve just described exactly why it\u2019s dodgy. John was lamenting how it kind of sucks that you don\u2019t have to care at all what the person you\u2019re trying to influence cares about because you just instill whatever intimacies you want and build off that, but depending on context of who you are and what they already believe that might just flat not work.<br /> <br /> Convincing 3 willpower 2 resolve farmer Joe of something is probably not going to be hard, but who cares, you\u2019re an exalt, your peers are gods and monsters, not random peasants. So let\u2019s say instead that you want to convince Ma-Ha-Suchi to commit his forces to join your fight against the Realm, but you have no, I mean absolutely zero, idea what his intimacies are. So you say to yourself \u201cwell who cares, I\u2019ll just instill an intimacy for \u2018tyranny is evil.\u2019 and work off that.\u201d Except, whoops, he\u2019s got a defining tie of \u201cI will raise up a new Lunar Realm where I am admired and respected by all.\u201d So no, he\u2019s not having any of your \u201cfreedom for all people\u201d BS. Tyrants are awesome, the problem is that he\u2019s not currently the biggest tyrant, and you better believe he\u2019s spending one of his 10 willpower to stop that intimacy from forming. You won\u2019t even know why you failed either, or that you had a way way easier avenue in his already defining intimacy of hatred for the usurpers. <br /> <br /> I would also say, admittedly this isn\u2019t codified in the rules, but that your personal standing with the person you\u2019re trying to convince matters too. If you\u2019re a Solar captured by the Wyld Hunt, you might try to convince your captors that the First and Forsaken Lion is a serious threat to the entire region and needs to be dealt with, and they might have no intimacies that directly oppose that, but if you\u2019re just trying to instill it based off the force of your personality, there\u2019s a good chance they\u2019ll just shake it off because anything out of the mouth of an anathema is not to be taken seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:52:23-08:00","id":1345849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345845#post1345845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But...you\u2019ve just described exactly why it\u2019s dodgy. John was lamenting how it kind of sucks that you don\u2019t have to care at all what the person you\u2019re trying to influence cares about because you just instill whatever intimacies you want and build off that, but depending on context of who you are and what they already believe that might just flat not work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sure as hell is dodgey, and that is what makes it realistic. There is a reason the term manipulative has negative connotations in English, people do try to cold sell you stuff all the time and yeah it does work sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:33:01-08:00","id":1345867,"title":"","content":"I think that the Intimacy system works as intended.<br /> In our Campaign, we evaluate Intimacies every few sessions and update them, adding and deleting, or modifying as the character grows and changes.<br /> Sometimes we even make suggestions on which Events may spark or modify Intimacies... <br /> Worked pretty well in my opinion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:18:16-08:00","id":1345887,"title":"","content":"In my games Minor intimacies come and go all the time, and they either grow into Major or erode depending on what happens after, an intimacy being created at Major happens, though it's rare. Defining intimacies changing or eroding usually means heavy duty character development is happening (for example is I have an intimacy of &quot;I will avenge my mother&quot; and I go through with the avenging that intimacy is probably going to see some changes).<br /> <br /> Although I have struggled with the issue of when to spend WP to block new intimacies, especially when STing and it's an NPCs being influenced. I kind of have some internal guidelines built from my experience, but I'd love to see how others handle it. On the one hand letting someone roll into a character's life and upturn it completely with a couple of rolls can be unfun, but so can blocking too many new intimacies and frustrating the players or the ST. I'd love to get people's thoughts on this (might make a new thread if people think it's appropriate)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12778-rustedair","name":"RustedAir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:44:54-08:00","id":1345906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345849#post1345849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sure as hell is dodgey, and that is what makes it realistic. There is a reason the term manipulative has negative connotations in English, people do try to cold sell you stuff all the time and yeah it does work sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue (from both a personal and business perspective) that cold selling generally appeals to what are assumed to be Intimacies. (Note to remember cultural intimacies below.) One that is prevalent today is, 'I want to be comfortable.' So someone 'cold selling' you a car might try a tack that it's more comfortable. Or, in another venue, most people who are applying for jobs are assumed to have an Intimacy, 'I want more money.' (That may be a derivative of, 'I want to be comfortable (and I need money to do that)'), but I think that is more of an indictment of our culture than anything else. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As a business example, my company is a tech company in a pretty small niche. I get weekly if not daily emails and even phone calls from tech providers who see that I am a tech company in this niche and they think that I can use their services. And I don't. This is a classic example of not having an Intimacy to support your Persuade action. If someone takes the time to understand my personal or professional Intimacies (you know, like Read Intentions), they would quickly realize this and not waste both of our time.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think that, in Exalted terms, cold selling is mainly a straight Persuade action with guessing of Intimacies based on cultural norms, and it has a success rate proportional to how prevalent that Intimacy is.<br /> <br /> On that note, something that would both help gameplay <i>and</i> work with Lunars is to explicitly model Cultural Intimacies. That is, there are Intimacies that can be assumed as part of a Culture. People of that Culture are more or less likely to have this Intimacy. You could also work to erode this Intimacy. I'm not looking at straitjackets, here, but something like this:<br /> <br /> Assume in contemporary American culture that there is an Intimacy of 'Government should not be trusted.' Now, not everyone has this Intimacy. In fact, someone may have the opposite Intimacy. However, they worked to overcome this. (That is, they are counterculture in this regard.) So instead of assuming that, except otherwise stated, someone's rating for an Intimacy is 0 (i.e., it doesn't exist), assume that someone's rating is whatever the culture's rating is. Then, adjust from there.<br /> <br /> Not only does this allow for the definition of culture in game terms, it would then be a system that works with Charms. A few Solar Charms (like Mastery of Small Manners) already dabble in this space. Lunar Social Charms have entire cascades dealing with manipulating Cultural Intimacies, but since they're not defined explicitly, it ends up feeling... weird.<br /> <br /> I dunno. This feels like it needs a bit more work, but this may help (me, at least) with fleshing out the system and working with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T15:29:37-08:00","id":1345922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RustedAir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345887#post1345887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games Minor intimacies come and go all the time, and they either grow into Major or erode depending on what happens after, an intimacy being created at Major happens, though it's rare. Defining intimacies changing or eroding usually means heavy duty character development is happening (for example is I have an intimacy of &quot;I will avenge my mother&quot; and I go through with the avenging that intimacy is probably going to see some changes).<br /> <br /> Although I have struggled with the issue of when to spend WP to block new intimacies, especially when STing and it's an NPCs being influenced. I kind of have some internal guidelines built from my experience, but I'd love to see how others handle it. On the one hand letting someone roll into a character's life and upturn it completely with a couple of rolls can be unfun, but so can blocking too many new intimacies and frustrating the players or the ST. I'd love to get people's thoughts on this (might make a new thread if people think it's appropriate)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Personally, I look at it this way: Would the instilled Intimacy go against a Defining Intimacy? If so, the character might as well spend themselves empty trying to resist that. Would the instilled Intimacy go against a Major Intimacy? Then they spend WP unless they're at half or less WP and don't feel like it's worth the exhaustion. Would it go against a Minor one? They spend WP if they're at full WP, but otherwise... nah, not worth.<br /> <br /> If it goes WITH another Intimacy, in a way that causes them to lose Resolve against the Influence, then it becomes increasingly difficult for them to resist with WP: Going against no Intimacy but upholding a Minor or greater Intimacy of theirs means they will not spend WP unless it would change their character concept significantly; the higher the upheld Intimacy is, the less inclined they'd be to resisting EVEN if it changes their concept. Going against and for equal-intensity Intimacies cancels each other out which means they might or might not resist based on context. Going against a higher Intimacy than the one you uphold or vice-versa: basically subtract one with the other, the result applies as if you were going for or against that. For example, going against a Defining but upholding a Minor is equivalent to going against a Major one flatly.<br /> <br /> Stuff like Psyche effects or other non-natural influence are treated on a case by case basis, but often resisted as soon as possible, which doesn't tend to be very soon. <br /> <br /> Just a very vague eyeballing of how I think about NPCs resisting or not, in the end just doing the fun thing works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:41:23-08:00","id":1345986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345906#post1345906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would argue (from both a personal and business perspective) that cold selling generally appeals to what are assumed to be Intimacies. (Note to remember cultural intimacies below.) One that is prevalent today is, 'I want to be comfortable.' So someone 'cold selling' you a car might try a tack that it's more comfortable. Or, in another venue, most people who are applying for jobs are assumed to have an Intimacy, 'I want more money.' (That may be a derivative of, 'I want to be comfortable (and I need money to do that)'), but I think that is more of an indictment of our culture than anything else. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're pretty much right. Any realistic person probably has dozens or even hundreds of Minor Intimacies that people should be able to play off of, kinda negating the cold sell arguement. It's a reason I tend to give characters tones of little intimacies. I don't just put down a religion, or philosophy, as an intimacy, I put down many different aspects of a religion at different levels to show what parts the character values. Cultural details get thrown in too. But if you aren't going to do that simply allowing the cold sell serves as an excellent shorthand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T05:41:23-08:00","id":1346137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345986#post1345986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're pretty much right. Any realistic person probably has dozens or even hundreds of Minor Intimacies that people should be able to play off of, kinda negating the cold sell arguement. It's a reason I tend to give characters tones of little intimacies. I don't just put down a religion, or philosophy, as an intimacy, I put down many different aspects of a religion at different levels to show what parts the character values. Cultural details get thrown in too. But if you aren't going to do that simply allowing the cold sell serves as an excellent shorthand.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More than once I've found myself in a situation where one of my players is trying to leverage an intimacy they haven't read, for one reason or another. And a lot of the time I'm like &quot;Well they don't have an intimacy for (for example) their district on their sheet, but it makes sense, so the influence is valid&quot;. Sort of improvising intimacies on the go because, as you said, a person would likely have a bunch of minor intimacies and maybe a major or two I hadn't thought of when writing them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12778-rustedair","name":"RustedAir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:19:41-08:00","id":1346179,"title":"","content":"Gotta say I'm loving the idea of cultural intimacies. You could even have the strength of it as how ingrained in their culture they are against how free thinking/iconoclastic they are. So You might have Lookshy culture as an intimacy. At defining level its a character defined by their patriotism, who has dedicated themselves to public service, works hard on living up to the public virtues of the people of Lookshy and probably looks down on those undisciplined rabble of the other Scavenger Land cities. At minor it might be someone who was born and raised in Lookshy but is more cosmopolitan, they've maybe travelled or read widely. They might hold their culture quite fondly while, for instance, also believing that other cities have their own virtues and that the Lookshy virtues aren't the only worthy ones. Appeals to their patriotism would be harder. Someone with a major intimacy might be fully inculcated in their culture but either hasn't questioned it sufficient for doubt, or who has questioned it and come to terms with some of its weaknesses, able to admit the occassional flaw in the people of Lookshy, but generally regarding the Lookshy way as superior. Someone with the intimacy at 0 (i.e. doesn't have it) might be indifferent having been raised outside of the public school system, such as by travellers or criminals. They might well understand the Lookshy virtues and might have them as intimacies seperately, but not see themselves as a patriot.<br /> <br /> I'd say that almost every character should probably have at least a minor cultural intimacy, unless they have a really good reason (raised in captivity, etc). Its hard, and not always desirable to shed what you learned through your upbringing, and most cultures have genuinely worthy virtues and cultural themes to believe in.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback all, this has been really helpful. I like the idea of throwing out minor intimacies willy-nilly and also of having a quick check with players every few sessions to see if they think any of their intimacies have changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:52:53-08:00","id":1346211,"title":"","content":"Gribble, I think you misunderstood me. I don't want Lookshy Culture (Respect) as a Tie. That tells me <i>nothing</i> about the Culture.<br /> <br /> I want Lookshy Culture to defined as a set of Intimacies:<br /> <br /> Military Structure (Trust) - Major<br /> The Scarlet Dynasty (Distrust) - Major<br /> The Scavenger Lands (Protective) - Minor<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> <br /> And then the <i>typical</i> character from Lookshy <i>has those Intimacies</i>. The fact of the matter is that the more Intimacies someone has, the better the Social System of Exalted works. There's a lot of complaints about Exalts just ignoring Intimacies and generating the ones they need. The most likely reason is that just coming up with a lot of Intimacies is time-consuming, sometimes difficult, and (for the players) often counter to what they want.<br /> <br /> And it should be noted that PC Intimacies are very often weaknesses. They're handles on a set of people that tend to <i>not</i> want handles. Well... how do you deal with that?<br /> <br /> It would also be a source of crunch in the books like The Realm and Across the Eight Directions. You could list some cultural Ties for each area discussed in those books. I realize that it's too late for the Realm, but it may be something to think about in the future...<br /> <br /> It also gives a pure <i>niche</i> for Lunar Social Combat. Solars create and manipulate Personal Intimacies. Lunars create and manipulate Cultural Intimacies.<br /> <br /> And, again, individuals can diverge from their Culture's Intimacies, but that should take effort. As an example, I've been rereading the Honor Harrington series, and in it the Solarian League's Office of Frontier Security would very clearly have a Cultural Intimacy of 'Corruption? What's that?' However, one OFS director, Oravil Barregos, is well known for the fact that he is <i>not</i> corrupt. This is just an example where someone diverges from the Culture.<br /> <br /> I can think of a lot of hooks that this could lead to, with the possible downside of being treated as a straitjacket. Even then, though, I think that are many other systems (and subsystems) in Exalted 3E that have a worse issue with this....<br /> <br /> Anyway, just trying to clarify my stance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:30:48-08:00","id":1346229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346211#post1346211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want Lookshy Culture (Respect) as a Tie. That tells me <i>nothing</i> about the Culture.<br /> <br /> I want Lookshy Culture to defined as a set of Intimacies:<br /> <br /> Military Structure (Trust) - Major<br /> The Scarlet Dynasty (Distrust) - Major<br /> The Scavenger Lands (Protective) - Minor<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> <br /> And then the <i>typical</i> character from Lookshy <i>has those Intimacies</i>.<br /> <br /> It would also be a source of crunch in the books like The Realm and Across the Eight Directions. You could list some cultural Ties for each area discussed in those books. I realize that it's too late for the Realm, but it may be something to think about in the future...<br /> <br /> Anyway, just trying to clarify my stance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty kickass stance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:53:51-08:00","id":1346237,"title":"","content":"I also like dividing generic cultural intimacies into more specific aspects of cultures but found hard to have the time and ideas to maintain good NPC quality","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:33:17-08:00","id":1346260,"title":"","content":"Also to answer the main topic (I will mainly repeat what others said so I guess we are now a Battle group of forum posters) :<br /> <br /> 1) Minor, and to a certain extent major, intimacies can change quite often, I'd say every character see 4-5 changes in intimacies or in inspire per session (like 1 person did a dance stuff, one person tried to threaten everyone because he was angry, there was RP between different characters and one tried to setup a bro bond with another because last time he helped him do one thing, this kind of stuff). Expecting less could become boring I think, but I don't know, some people seems to have different experiences<br /> <br /> 2) All intimacies are not noted on the character sheet. It has been said intimacies not strong enough might not be noted. I would like to nuance this ; I rather think of intimacies as narrative indicator of what kind of topics makes sense to involve the character in the story, so some extremely important cornerstone of a character might not be noted as a Defining intimacy if they are not narratively relevant. For example, I think lots of characters I have seen could certainly have a Major or Defining intimacy of love to their parents (If I threw their parents in mortal dangers, I'm pretty sure lots of characters I've seen would travel the world to try to save them), but they had no intimacy related to this. To me, it informs the ST and other players that this is not relevant for the story (despite the character personal feelings). It doesn't mean another character should never use these &quot;hidden&quot; intimacies as a leverage, but rather that it should not be considered the go-to solution because concerned players are likely not interested in it. I think I'm influenced seeing intimacies like them with the work of aspirations from the last Chronicles of Darkness games, I really liked these mechanics.<br /> <br /> 3) Finally, every few scenes, I would propose players to take 15 ins to look at their intimacies and tell me if they felt it was still relevant to their character, and with en intensity that make sense. It also allows to eliminate intimacies that have no more purpose because the story changed.<br /> <br /> Overall I think being around 10 intimacies is good (no need to start at 10, but expect lots of people to at least come close to 10 after few sessions of play even if they start at the 4 mandatory). I would never go beyond 15, and I would advise my players to not go there as well. But it's only my advice, I totally get that some people love to have a lot of intimacies. However, I think with too many of them it becomes more and more incompatible with any intent to have a focus on strong narration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:40:33-08:00","id":1346265,"title":"","content":"I think that i have just over a dozen each (Principle and Tie)... But then, I do think that there should likely be more, but many of them are just not narratively all that important most of the time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:49:25-08:00","id":1346269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346265#post1346265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that i have just over a dozen each (Principle and Tie)... But then, I do think that there should likely be more, but many of them are just not narratively all that important most of the time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think this one really depends on your relation to RPGs and narration. <br /> <br /> Me of few years ago would never get enough intimacies I guess.<br /> <br /> In the meantime though, I discovered content creators talking a lot about cinema and narration (my personal favorites are Just Write, Lindsey Eillis, Patrick H Willems, but everyone got their taste I won't even try to convince anyone) and now I can't stop thinking about narrative elements in my games. But I don't think this choice makes a better story per itself. It just makes a story I relate to more easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T23:52:57-08:00","id":1346387,"title":"","content":"In the games I've run and played in, I've seen some significant intimacy changes. I've never seen a defining intimacy go down, but the PC I played ended up with a minor tie to his familiar developing into a defining one. He certainly developed a couple of major intimacies, and a host of minor ones. In the game I run, I've definitely managed to develop intimacies up to the major level in PCs mostly through the work of NPCs to persuade them. In most cases they're ones that the character could have spent willpower on avoiding, but which the player thought would be an interesting turn for the character. Ones like that usually remain at the minor level. And other times when I'm ST-ing I might ask something like, &quot;You've spent a lot of time around this NPC. Have you developed an intimacy towards them?&quot; Usually even if it happens immediately before a roll that might leverage it, my players are honest about it. The only ones they're adamant about refusing are ones that I'm obviously going to try to use against them later (Makarios is trying to instill a Principle of &quot;I lust for Makarios' goods&quot;).<br /> <br /> And there's always the option to just try to persuade someone based on an intimacy you guess that they have, even without a Read Intentions roll. It's a risky option, especially if you try to boost the roll with charms, since even with a gazillion successes the attempt might be unsuccessful if the intimacy you're banking on isn't there. But if their Guile is high, it might be the only way to glean information about someone's intimacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11685-sundance","name":"Sundance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T00:24:45-08:00","id":1346393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345823#post1345823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the Red Rule, that's just... the rule. &quot;Any seduction attempt that violates a character's sexual orientation (as defined by the player, or by the Storyteller in the case of Storyteller characters) is unacceptable [influence]&quot;.<br /> <br /> Playing a failed social action as forming a contrary Intimacy to represent a lowered opinion is fine, but folding that into the general social system seems far too unwieldy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except against Rose Lipped Seduction Style I suppose (which explicitly overcomes Unacceptable Influences) but that can still be nixed by the Red Rule.<br /> <br /> Makes me feel kind of bad for optimized Black Claw Stylists that 40% of the Juju you-do can be arbitrarily no selled by every other player at the table including the ST. (As in you can make 4 reflexive social influences a turn, but half of them get stopped by the Red Rule) But that\u2019s part of the Storytelling social compact, I would imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 11-06-2019, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T04:28:35-08:00","id":1346420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346393#post1346393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except against Rose Lipped Seduction Style I suppose (which explicitly overcomes Unacceptable Influences) but that can still be nixed by the Red Rule.<br /> <br /> Makes me feel kind of bad for optimized Black Claw Stylists that 40% of the Juju you-do can be arbitrarily no selled by every other player at the table including the ST. (As in you can make 4 reflexive social influences a turn, but half of them get stopped by the Red Rule) But that\u2019s part of the Storytelling social compact, I would imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the social system gives players a lot of control and assumes that your not going to get into social fu fights with each other in bad faith. ...also yeah, the DARVO MA having some intense limiters on its use in PvP seems appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T04:42:53-08:00","id":1346422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346420#post1346420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the social system gives players a lot of control and assumes that your not going to get into social fu fights with each other in bad faith. ...also yeah, the DARVO MA having some intense limiters on its use in PvP seems appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and really it's not your party I'm concerned about really, but if your ST is going to tell you that all the DB warriors you go up against are immune to your charms because of Red Rule, I'd roll up another character concept. Like one of the ones that go straight to eviscerating.<br /> <br /> prototype00<br /> <br /> Edit: If it isn't clear, I am talking about NPCs here, only thats not really true as the ST is also considered a player and all NPCs can thus invoke the Red Rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 11-06-2019, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T04:53:02-08:00","id":1346424,"title":"","content":"If I may roll things back for a moment, I want to just address an appalling but of slander:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1345845#post1345845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let\u2019s say instead that you want to convince Ma-Ha-Suchi to commit his forces to join your fight against the Realm, but you have no, I mean absolutely zero, idea what his intimacies are. So you say to yourself \u201cwell who cares, I\u2019ll just instill an intimacy for \u2018tyranny is evil.\u2019 and work off that.\u201d Except, whoops, he\u2019s got a defining tie of \u201cI will raise up a new Lunar Realm where I am admired and respected by all.\u201d So no, he\u2019s not having any of your \u201cfreedom for all people\u201d BS. Tyrants are awesome, the problem is that he\u2019s not currently the biggest tyrant, and you better believe he\u2019s spending one of his 10 willpower to stop that intimacy from forming. </div> </div> </div> </div>Ma-Ha-Suchi hangs around with a trio of mortal leaders who are engaged with as equals, over a system of government that encourages things like playing peaks on him.<br /> <br /> Wanting to be admired and respected by all hardly makes one a tyrant.<br /> <br /> Besides, a character who actually was a tyrant could still be instilled with that Intimacy of they don't actually think of themselves as one. Gul Dukat would absolutely agree with you that tyrants are evil, while also providing a litany of justifications and rationalisations for himself.<br /> <br /> And why does the Principle suddenly turn from &quot;tyrants are evil&quot; to &quot;freedom for all people&quot;? Those aren't the same thing at all (and I certainly hardly see why the desire to be admired and respected results in wanting to deny freedoms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T04:56:10-08:00","id":1346425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346393#post1346393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except against Rose Lipped Seduction Style I suppose (which explicitly overcomes Unacceptable Influences) but that can still be nixed by the Red Rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes me feel kind of bad for optimized Black Claw Stylists that 40% of the Juju you-do can be arbitrarily no selled by every other player at the table including the ST. (As in you can make 4 reflexive social influences a turn, but half of them get stopped by the Red Rule) But that\u2019s part of the Storytelling social compact, I would imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I think you may have misread a good deal of that style.<br /> <br /> Also, we're talking about maintaining people's comfort zones regarding the subject of sexual agency, let's try and not characterise that as arbitrary shall we?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T05:06:07-08:00","id":1346428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346425#post1346425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No. I think you may have misread a good deal of that style.<br /> <br /> Also, we're talking about maintaining people's comfort zones regarding the subject of sexual agency, let's try and not characterise that as arbitrary shall we?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, thats another bit of slander, lol. I think about Martial Arts Styles a great deal. Just look up Maiden of the Black Claw, thats one of the concepts I'm kind of pleased with.<br /> <br /> Black Claw lets you instill like crazy, intimacies that you are weak, delicate, a beautiful flower being crushed under an unyielding heel. And you can use those newly formed Intimacies to re-inforce an intimacy of Attraction/Lust using Thousand Courtesan Ways.<br /> <br /> With poised lion you also get a free social action once per round which can be doubled with Thousand Courtesan Ways.<br /> <br /> All uses of Thousand Courtesan Ways are subject to the Red Rule.<br /> <br /> The upshot of it is that by the end of a couple of round of combat, you've got most foes wrapped around your pinkie, socially speaking, except if Red Rule. And if they want to spend willpower on it, great! Less for them when you land your no-targeted intimacy persuasion targeting their raging hormones (lets you and I finish this in private in that town we saw on the way, handsome/beautiful, leave your army behind, they'll keep, promise.).<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 11-06-2019, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T05:13:09-08:00","id":1346429,"title":"","content":"Black Claw simply keys off of positive Intimacies, it does not mandate that those Intimacies have to be lust or love based.<br /> <br /> If your ST assaults your Black Claw lady with 4 gay DBs, you can still make them fiercely protective/respectful/awed/adoring of the stylist without there being any sexual attraction involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T05:18:28-08:00","id":1346430,"title":"","content":"On the seduction example given, I think that if your player approaches and tries to seduce a sexually non-compatible NPC and gets 23 successes, sure they aren't going to seduce that person, but as a GM I'd certainly rule that a similar non-sexual intimacy might happen instead, with the players consent.<br /> <br /> I mean, think about it in narrative terms. You are approached by the smoothest and most delightful person of all time who flatters you and makes you feel special. Sure you don't want to do the nasty with them, but you'd feel something and it wouldn't be anger (unless you have some kind of intimacy that would translate that into anger). I mean I feel great if a gay guy compliments me, even though there is 0% chance of him getting lucky. And thats some average guy in a club/bar. 23 successes represents a level of smoothness, cool and sheer seductive awesomeness that is literally godlike. A botch might result in anger, but lots of successes? I'd GM that into something like<br /> &quot;You make an offhand compliment about his fetching outfit and after a short and enjoyable chat you feel that he isn't responding to your advances at all, however, given you've rolled really well, you manage to turn it into a friendly chat about his tailor and how good the outfit makes him look. You deftly extract yourself from the conversation some minutes later. Since you didn't manage to instill a lust intimacy, but you made a really good impression, would you like to instill a minor intimacy of well disposed to &lt;your character&gt; instead?&quot;<br /> <br /> On the cultural intimacies, I can see the wisdom of breaking the cultures down into a set of specific intimacies, not least because you won't need to remember/have separate lists of what each cultural intimacy means. I think it should probably be more of a buffet approach though.<br /> Sticking with the example of Lookshy, maybe<br /> Respect for the military<br /> Respect for public service<br /> Disdain for self centred advancement<br /> Protectiveness to the scavenger lands with Lookshy as a benevolent guardian<br /> Disdain for the Realm as a hostile aggressor<br /> <br /> and then let the PCs choose what strength they have for each and whether there are any they think are inappropriate for their character. So a merchant of lookshy might be fine with self centred personal advancement (while understanding its somewhat frowned upon) and not have it as a intimacy, but might be very keen on protection of the scavenger lands and hence support for the military, mayeb because they believe that trade suffers when an area is too unsafe to travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T05:20:53-08:00","id":1346432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346429#post1346429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Claw simply keys off of positive Intimacies, it does not mandate that those Intimacies have to be lust or love based.<br /> <br /> If your ST assaults your Black Claw lady with 4 gay DBs, you can still make them fiercely protective/respectful/awed/adoring of the stylist without there being any sexual attraction involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes agreed, but 2 mechanistic things:<br /> <br /> 1. Thousand Courtesan Ways is one of the most efficient social effect generators in the game.<br /> <br /> 2. Rose Lipped Seduction Style explicitly (as stated) can make there be sexual attraction where there wasn't any (and indeed where it is an Unacceptable Influence, basically the strongest anti-social effect in the game, prior to Red-Ruling).<br /> <br /> So if one of the most efficient ways to use it is to use your torn innocence to entice and seduce others, I don't see that there is anything particularly incongruous about that. However, of course, Red Rule, as stated previously, on the part of the ST can mean that you shouldn't/can't play that way.<br /> <br /> prototype00<br /> <br /> Edit: Of course, really what you are trying to do is get that Lust/Attraction Intimacy up to Defining and then Heart Ripping Claw them, ha!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 11-06-2019, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T05:40:35-08:00","id":1346436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346432#post1346432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes agreed, but 2 mechanistic things:<br /> <br /> 1. Thousand Courtesan Ways is one of the most efficient social effect generators in the game.<br /> <br /> 2. Rose Lipped Seduction Style explicitly (as stated) can make there be sexual attraction where there wasn't any (and indeed where it is an Unacceptable Influence, basically the strongest anti-social effect in the game, prior to Red-Ruling).<br /> <br /> So if one of the most efficient ways to use it is to use your torn innocence to entice and seduce others, I don't see that there is anything particularly incongruous about that. However, of course, Red Rule, as stated previously, on the part of the ST can mean that you shouldn't/can't play that way.<br /> <br /> prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div>You're gonna refuse to play Black Claw just because you can't use Rose Lipped Seduction Style? That's your choice, but I strongly disagree that this single-handedly makes Black Claw not worth using.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T05:43:21-08:00","id":1346437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346436#post1346436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're gonna refuse to play Black Claw just because you can't use Rose Lipped Seduction Style? That's your choice, but I strongly disagree that this single-handedly makes Black Claw not worth using.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm not personally, as I don't have any games on at the moment where I'm running this character.<br /> <br /> But if I was to give honest advice, if the ST is a big stickler for the Red Rule for NPCs, I'd advise a gamer bud to try something more directly eviscerating, as stated upthread. Like Death Kitty or whatnot. I don't personally enjoy not being able to access a bunch of effects that make a character concept really hum.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T06:26:18-08:00","id":1346444,"title":"","content":"I've opinions on the Red Rule that I wont both sharing, none positive.<br /> <br /> What is more relevant is the rules concerning Sexual Orientation. I personally feel that treating sexual orientation as an intimacy rather than a solid immutable concept. Is much more fitting for the setting. Creation really comes across as a place which people are more sexually fluid. In particular when a weak willed individual is faced with the overwhelming might of an Exalt. If it really matters that much make a charactrr's sexual orientation a Defining Intimacy, this thread suggests that nobody has seen a Defining Intimacy fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T06:38:17-08:00","id":1346447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346437#post1346437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if I was to give honest advice, if the ST is a big stickler for the Red Rule for NPCs...</div> </div> </div> </div>People who invoke the Red Rule aren't being &quot;sticklers.&quot; <i>They have lines they don't want crossed</i>\u200b. I consider myself reasonably open-minded, but there are some character types I just would not be comfortable RPing a seduction scene with.<br /> <br /> \u200bIntentionally suggesting that players instead play a character who &quot;goes straight to eviscerating&quot; as revenge against the ST being uncomfortable with seduction, is not good table behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T06:44:03-08:00","id":1346448,"title":"","content":"The appropriate response to being uncomfortable roleplaying a seduction if to let the dice do most of the talking and fade to black for the action.<br /> <br /> If you dont want to do any sexual stuff you establish it up front then everyone can make appropriate characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T06:47:47-08:00","id":1346449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346448#post1346448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you dont want to do any sexual stuff you establish it up front then everyone can make appropriate characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that <i>regardless of whether anyone is uncomfortable with sexual stuff or not</i>, everyone should have a talk up front so as to make appropriate characters.<br /> <br /> (But I also still preserve the Red Rule because you don't always know you're going to be uncomfortable with something until you encounter it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-06-2019, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T06:51:38-08:00","id":1346450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346447#post1346447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who invoke the Red Rule aren't being &quot;sticklers.&quot; <i>They have lines they don't want crossed</i>\u200b. I consider myself reasonably open-minded, but there are some character types I just would not be comfortable RPing a seduction scene with.<br /> <br /> \u200bIntentionally suggesting that players instead play a character who &quot;goes straight to eviscerating&quot; as revenge against the ST being uncomfortable with seduction, is not good table behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand me. I want all the characters I play to be able to make full use of the rules to do what they do.<br /> <br /> Suggesting that someone plays one of my builds that I've built to KILL THINGS is not an act of revenge against the Storyteller, its suggesting that instead of playing a build where you can't use 50% of the tools to do things to instead play a build that is pumping on all cylinders all the time. Like I said, I don't enjoy being hamstrung (as I would imagine most people would not).<br /> <br /> If the hamstringing occurs in the name of boundaries and personal comfort levels, well and good, play another concept that won't affect other people negatively. The reason I suggest evisceration is that unlike the Red Rule, there is nothing in the rules (except the Orichalcum Rule, but that one is all encompassing) that bars a player from being superlatively good at the combat mechanics. But really it could be anything, just be y'know Exalted and really good at it.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T07:23:37-08:00","id":1346451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346447#post1346447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who invoke the Red Rule aren't being &amp;quot;sticklers.&amp;quot; <i>They have lines they don't want crossed</i>\u200b. I consider myself reasonably open-minded, but there are some character types I just would not be comfortable RPing a seduction scene with.<br /> <br /> \u200bIntentionally suggesting that players instead play a character who &amp;quot;goes straight to eviscerating&amp;quot; as revenge against the ST being uncomfortable with seduction, is not good table behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are uncomfortable with me bringing a seducer to your table, but you are comfortable with graphic violence at your table, then me bringing a murderhobo isn't &quot;revenge&quot; -- it's me respecting the boundaries you set at your table.<br /> <br /> (If you can't handle violence or sexual themes then I wish you well but I do not want to play Exalted with you -- and I guarentee you don't want to play with me.)<br /> <br /> Personally, were I playing with someone uncomfortable with sexual themes, I'd houserule that all the Love and Lust effects are refluffed as Platonic Friendship. Celestial Bliss Trick means you have a three minute gossip about the weather that leads to a Defining Tie of Platonic Friendship. That way social builds aren't hilariously hindered and no-one gets squicked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T07:24:29-08:00","id":1346452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346428#post1346428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, thats another bit of slander, lol. I think about Martial Arts Styles a great deal. Just look up Maiden of the Black Claw, thats one of the concepts I'm kind of pleased with.<br /> <br /> Black Claw lets you instill like crazy, intimacies that you are weak, delicate, a beautiful flower being crushed under an unyielding heel. And you can use those newly formed Intimacies to re-inforce an intimacy of Attraction/Lust using Thousand Courtesan Ways.<br /> <br /> With poised lion you also get a free social action once per round which can be doubled with Thousand Courtesan Ways.<br /> <br /> All uses of Thousand Courtesan Ways are subject to the Red Rule.<br /> <br /> The upshot of it is that by the end of a couple of round of combat, you've got most foes wrapped around your pinkie, socially speaking, except if Red Rule. And if they want to spend willpower on it, great! Less for them when you land your no-targeted intimacy persuasion targeting their raging hormones (lets you and I finish this in private in that town we saw on the way, handsome/beautiful, leave your army behind, they'll keep, promise.).<br /> <br /> prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346432#post1346432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes agreed, but 2 mechanistic things:<br /> <br /> 1. Thousand Courtesan Ways is one of the most efficient social effect generators in the game.<br /> <br /> 2. Rose Lipped Seduction Style explicitly (as stated) can make there be sexual attraction where there wasn't any (and indeed where it is an Unacceptable Influence, basically the strongest anti-social effect in the game, prior to Red-Ruling).<br /> <br /> So if one of the most efficient ways to use it is to use your torn innocence to entice and seduce others, I don't see that there is anything particularly incongruous about that. However, of course, Red Rule, as stated previously, on the part of the ST can mean that you shouldn't/can't play that way.<br /> <br /> prototype00<br /> <br /> Edit: Of course, really what you are trying to do is get that Lust/Attraction Intimacy up to Defining and then Heart Ripping Claw them, ha!</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346437#post1346437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'm not personally, as I don't have any games on at the moment where I'm running this character.<br /> <br /> But if I was to give honest advice, if the ST is a big stickler for the Red Rule for NPCs, I'd advise a gamer bud to try something more directly eviscerating, as stated upthread. Like Death Kitty or whatnot. I don't personally enjoy not being able to access a bunch of effects that make a character concept really hum.<br /> <br /> prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div>Rrrriiiiggghhhhtttt, so you don't so much feel bad for &quot;optimized Black Claw Stylists&quot; as you do for your own self and your fairly idiosyncratic and specific needs for the Style. The idea of applying it towards character concepts and scenarios other than seduction is something you consider not worth your time.<br /> <br /> And you not only imagine that any Storyteller that would frequently respond to such action with the Red Rule would be doing so antagonistically, but make cutesy little jokes about how you would respond to such antagonism in kind with depictions of extreme violence.<br /> <br /> A purely hypothetical Storyteller of course, meaning you're also imagining persecution where none exists, but not hypothesizing that maybe a Storyteller who would respond in such a manner has some kind of... trauma?<br /> <br /> Yyyyikes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creation really comes across as a place which people are more sexually fluid. In particular when a weak willed individual is faced with the overwhelming might on an Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>All right, first, that's not how sexuality works.<br /> <br /> Second, the Exalted capacity to be seductive across a person's usual lines of sexuality is already covered in a Charm, as is virtually everything that makes the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Third, framing this subject in terms of overwhelming might exerted against weak willed people? That's, errr, that's also going to be a fucking Yikes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T07:32:35-08:00","id":1346453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346451#post1346451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you are uncomfortable with me bringing a seducer to your table, but you are comfortable with graphic violence at your table, then me bringing a murderhobo isn't &quot;revenge&quot; -- it's me respecting the boundaries you set at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I suspect that there are people who might even be okay with depictions of graphic violence in play up until the point where they get the impression that it's something being brought to the fore as a deliberate response to them invoking the Red Rule to make some kind of statement, because even if the violence on its own would not have distressed them, the attitude of harassment from a person on the other side of a table or computer monitor might very well.<br /> <br /> Let's not be discrete about the whole subject; the Red Rule is there so that the game's typical genre conceits around the subject of sexual interactions can give consideration for the fact that a very large section of people have some sexual trauma in their proximity, either from their own experience or that of a loved one. Like, a good deal more than have direct personal experiences of violence (notwithstanding the fact that Exalted often goes for a form of over-the-top or stylized violence which creates a further layer of separation from real life that people can more readily engage in).<br /> <br /> A person who does not give consideration for those things? Yeah, I absolutely agree that they shouldn't go anywhere near somebody who needs to safeguard those boundaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T07:34:38-08:00","id":1346454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346452#post1346452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rrrriiiiggghhhhtttt, so you don't so much feel bad for &quot;optimized Black Claw Stylists&quot; as you do for your own self and your fairly idiosyncratic and specific needs for the Style. The idea of applying it towards character concepts and scenarios other than seduction is something you consider not worth your time.<br /> <br /> And you not only imagine that any Storyteller that would frequently respond to such action with the Red Rule would be doing so antagonistically, but make cutesy little jokes about how you would respond to such antagonism in kind with depictions of extreme violence.<br /> <br /> A purely hypothetical Storyteller of course, meaning you're also imagining persecution where none exists, but not hypothesizing that maybe a Storyteller who would respond in such a manner has some kind of... trauma?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isator, I'd like to write a long post to respond, but I can't really be arsed. You're always playing the agent provocateur and getting away with it only because you make the other party angry enough to catch the falling mod hammer before you do.<br /> <br /> Not this time, my friend.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 11-06-2019, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T07:49:05-08:00","id":1346455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346453#post1346453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A person who does not give consideration for those things? Yeah, I absolutely agree that they shouldn't go anywhere near somebody who needs to safeguard those boundaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm always pleased when we agree.<br /> <br /> If you specifically don't want a kind of play at your table, and the other players respond by specifically not bringing that kind of play to your table then that's not a bad thing. <br /> <br /> You can perform whatever kind of contortion you like to that logic, but my respecting your boundaries is not a bad thing. <br /> <br /> Of course this is all (yikes) hypothetical. Imagining persecution where none exists. That sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T07:53:41-08:00","id":1346456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346452#post1346452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right, first, that's not how sexuality works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because everyone I've ever met doesnt exist. Unless, you're saying there are Exalts in the real world twisting people's sexual orientations.<br /> <br /> More relevant, as I said it's a setting thing. The setting is loaded with characters that are into pretty much everything.<br /> <br /> Also yes yikes. The setting is incredibly cynical about people and power. Take that away and you just have shiney people hitting eachother with surfboard sized swords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T08:51:00-08:00","id":1346467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346456#post1346456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, because everyone I've ever met doesnt exist. Unless, you're saying there are Exalts in the real world twisting people's sexual orientations.<br /> <br /> More relevant, as I said it's a setting thing. The setting is loaded with characters that are into pretty much everything.<br /> <br /> Also yes yikes. The setting is incredibly cynical about people and power. Take that away and you just have shiney people hitting eachother with surfboard sized swords.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no lore that supports the notion that humans in creation are all able to become attracted to anyone sufficiently &quot;powerful&quot;.<br /> <br /> 3e has moved away from 2e's style of using shock value with no regard for the message it sends as a result.<br /> <br /> If everyone at your table thinks Creation's humans should have malleable orientations, feel free to Orichalchum rule it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T10:53:13-08:00","id":1346509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346455#post1346455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you specifically don't want a kind of play at your table, and the other players respond by specifically not bringing that kind of play to your table then that's not a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn't.<br /> <br /> Bringing an alternative form of play that has been passed in terms of being a kind of punishment is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">my respecting your boundaries is not a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Acting in the manner proposed in this thread is not respectful of boundaries in an ingenuous manner.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course this is all (yikes) hypothetical. Imagining persecution where none exists. That sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't exist in the sense that people saying they would do it have not yet gotten the opportunity, sure.<br /> <br /> If I did see a person saying that they would use the Red Rule to shut down all attempts to leverage the Intimacies created with Black Claw Style for sexual purposes... well, ascertain why first. I wouldn't necessarily presume that they've had difficult experiences in the past (of a kind that have greater real world significance than how much one was allowed to optimise game rules), but it's a possibility worth considering and respecting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346456#post1346456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, because everyone I've ever met doesnt exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're a better judge than I on if you've only ever met people between 2 and 5 on the Kinsey scale, but there's a bigger world out there, it consists of plenty of 1s, 6s and asexual people, and their sexual feelings aren't really mutable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting is loaded with characters that are into pretty much everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has a few. More than many settings would give consideration to. The exact number has always been greatly exaggerated within the fandom. I find a lot of the ways in which people have talked about the whole &quot;everybody in Creation is bi&quot; to be informed by wider attitudes that are not respectful to bisexual people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting is incredibly cynical about people and power. Take that away and you just have shiney people hitting eachother with surfboard sized swords.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few things to unpack in this.<br /> <br /> One is that this Edition is the least cynical about that. I referred to Ma-Ha-Suchi earlier, and he's not the only Lunar in that book who interacts in a less absolute manner with people. Fangs at the Gate depicts a number of rich, engaging social scenarios that wouldn't exist in any other setting while still being predicated on images of power being employed responsibly and respectfully.<br /> <br /> You still brought presumptions about people and power that were framed not merely as things present in the game, but how you would expect people to act and things that ought to be in the game. As well as just general ideas of how sexual interplay works out; framing seduction in terms of something that a person has to and fails to resist because of a weak fortitude that is inflicted upon them by another is not merely weird and outputting, it's extremely narrow. It should not be at the core of anybody's argument about how these things work in the game.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that nobody can ever play a bastard character who acts like that with people, but it shouldn't be considered the default and it has issues that need to be managed carefully.<br /> <br /> Consent is something that is essential to sexual interaction; if not more than many other kinds of social activity, then at least something that has a long ugly history of being treated as less than. Even the best game rules will have difficulty making it feel as though consent is being portrayed credibly when the mechanics are still predicated on an actor leveraging resources against a passive target, finding the precise sequence of actions and phrases that unlocks a sexual response. Even if this is not what it is in the fiction, it's close enough to reasonably feel murky to people that have good cause to be really cautious about the matter of consent. That's not just people with direct or indirect traumas, who are undeniably a part of the hobby (an increasingly vocal part); we all benefit from continuously reinforcing that consent is paramount.<br /> <br /> So the Red Rule is there to serve as the final word on it, the final line to establish or deny consent, with the statement that players and Storytellers respect that.<br /> <br /> The concerns that somebody might playact withholding consent for mechanical advantage, or to deny another player the same? Well, I suppose that somewhere out there in the hobby there's somebody who's weird enough about playing games to do that, but they shouldn't really be the primary concern in discussing the idea. They're an outlier that should be dealt with in a case by case basis, not a basis for arguing the removal of a system of giving project to establishing consent.<br /> <br /> And I want to say outright that I find prioritizing the optimization of one's build over the value of that boundary is not a good look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T11:27:05-08:00","id":1346521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346509#post1346509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it isn't.<br /> <br /> Bringing an alternative form of play that has been passed in terms of being a kind of punishment is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Been passed in those terms by whom? None of the people suggesting an alternative form of play.<br /> <br /> I think you need to go back and read what's actually being said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346509#post1346509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acting in the manner proposed in this thread is not respectful of boundaries in an ingenuous manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>No-one is proposing that outside of a paranoid, disingenuous strawman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346509#post1346509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didn't exist in the sense that people saying they would do it have not yet gotten the opportunity, sure.<br /> <br /> If I did see a person saying that they would use the Red Rule to shut down all attempts to leverage the Intimacies created with Black Claw Style for sexual purposes... well, ascertain why first. I wouldn't necessarily presume that they've had difficult experiences in the past (of a kind that have greater real world significance than how much one was allowed to optimise game rules), but it's a possibility worth considering and respecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great. As I said, it's nice when we agree.<br /> <br /> I'd go a step further and say that if someone wanted to change their character because it was making people uncomfortable, I wouldn't necessarily presume that they're doing so as a convoluted attempt to ingenuously make people more uncomfortable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T11:39:54-08:00","id":1346525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The setting is loaded with characters that are into pretty much everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably worth pointing out that the writers of 1st ed felt that most rpgs were hostile to LGBT people, and they wanted to highlight LGBT people in-setting.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's supposed to be that there's more LGBT people than the real world. It's that a)most settings have an unrealistically low number of LGBT people, and b)an effort is made to highlight LGBT people.<br /> <br /> So if you <i>notice</i> a very high number of LGBT people, then this does not necessarily mean the setting <i>has</i> an extremely high number of LGBT people.<br /> <br /> It may just be the writers are trying to highlight them. It may be that it only seems high to you because you're used to reading fiction that avoids showing LGBT people (I obviously don't know what rpgs+fiction you normally read Hark, maybe it's not like these. I'm just making a general point, rather than about you particularly.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T11:49:51-08:00","id":1346529,"title":"","content":"And, more importantly... some of you guys are getting a bit personal. Lots of people accusing each other of having bad motives. Maybe you should dial it down a bit, make it less personal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T04:15:22-08:00","id":1346975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346525#post1346525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's probably worth pointing out that the writers of 1st ed felt that most rpgs were hostile to LGBT people, and they wanted to highlight LGBT people in-setting.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's supposed to be that there's more LGBT people than the real world. It's that a)most settings have an unrealistically low number of LGBT people, and b)an effort is made to highlight LGBT people.<br /> <br /> So if you <i>notice</i> a very high number of LGBT people, then this does not necessarily mean the setting <i>has</i> an extremely high number of LGBT people.<br /> <br /> It may just be the writers are trying to highlight them. It may be that it only seems high to you because you're used to reading fiction that avoids showing LGBT people (I obviously don't know what rpgs+fiction you normally read Hark, maybe it's not like these. I'm just making a general point, rather than about you particularly.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair. MoEP: Dragon-Blooded did genuinely draw a correlation between the epic libidos of the Terrestrial Exalted and homosexuality.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: Dragon-Blooded pg 50</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal women might have been forbidden to the lusty Dragon-Blooded men but everyone (and everything) else was fair game, and historians claim that the frequency of homosexual relations among the Dragon-Blooded dates back to this period.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's so fucking stupid it hurts, but it is canon and helped inform some people's ideas of the setting. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T12:39:44-08:00","id":1347315,"title":"","content":"I add new intimacies and remove others basically every scene. I tend to do short backstory and use the Intimacy list to describe my characters, so they have lots of hooks to use and also has lots to resist stuff. Major and Definig ones are a lot more restricted, but they Minor Intimimacies out the wazoo as people and things affect her and she grows through the game. <br /> <br /> Possibly a bit too loose, but it works for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T16:20:55-08:00","id":1347785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1347315#post1347315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I add new intimacies and remove others basically every scene. I tend to do short backstory and use the Intimacy list to describe my characters, so they have lots of hooks to use and also has lots to resist stuff. Major and Definig ones are a lot more restricted, but they Minor Intimimacies out the wazoo as people and things affect her and she grows through the game.<br /> <br /> Possibly a bit too loose, but it works for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i><b>EVERY SCENE</b></i>? Wow... that is a lot of Intimacy Manipulations...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T00:07:29-08:00","id":1347842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1346975#post1346975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair. MoEP: Dragon-Blooded did genuinely draw a correlation between the epic libidos of the Terrestrial Exalted and homosexuality.<br /> It's so fucking stupid it hurts, but it is canon and helped inform some people's ideas of the setting. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's stupid and the idea of greater prevelance of homosexuality actually comes from 1E:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted The Dragon-Blooded</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homosexuality is quite prevelant among the Dragon-Blooded, and it's considered quite acceptable to take same-sex lovers. If anything, it's easier to do because they don't have to worry about conception giving them away.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T07:13:42-08:00","id":1347885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1345779-intimacies-and-how-commonly-do-they-change?p=1347842#post1347842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's stupid and the idea of greater prevelance of homosexuality actually comes from 1E:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're entitled to your opinion but the context of the two quotes is completely different. One's talking about a social context in the Realm that's more forgiving towards homosexuality resulting in more homosexuality being expressed. The other is conflating the sexual orientations of modern Dragon-Blooded (not Dynasts) with the fact that their ancient ancestors were made to breed and forbidden from having sex with mortals.<br /> <br /> They had the same intention of saying you're allowed to play a gay character but while 1E was the Realm taking a few cultural nods from Pre-Meiji Japan, 2E generalising things and making it part of the Dragon-Blooded's DNA leans towards &quot;Creation is a world of gay!&quot; vs. &quot;Exalted isn't afraid to portray homosexuality&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 11-12-2019, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}